  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 409 AM MDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nOur upper level ridge starts to break down as the Low continues\nto push inward from the Pacific Northwest. The low starts to \nmove northward over our ridge as it moves into Montana/Canadian \nProvidences to the north of us. This low will continue to push \nshortwaves through our region Monday and Tuesday for afternoon \nand evening showers. The ridge starts to build back over us \nWednesday and THursday starting a drying period as we go into a \nmore westerly downsloping flow. The global models show the upper\nlevel low over the hudson bay area at this time which is far \nenough east to not influence the weather pattern over us. \nHowever, each of the global models do want to bring in another \nsystem into the Pacific Northwest at the end of the week so more\nprecipitation may be on the way next weekend we just will have \nto wait to see how the models trend.",
